  "post": {
    "caption": "The World Cup trophy is hollow gold. In 1970, Brazil won a third World Cup and kept the old trophy, so FIFA needed a new one. The Italian sculptor Silvio Gazzaniga won the design contest. His trophy is 18 karat gold and hollow inside, with two bands of green malachite around its base. West Germany lifted it first, in 1974. Winners do not keep it and get a replica instead. The real one stays at the FIFA Museum in Zurich. After Germany's 2014 win, the base was altered to make room for names, and the engraving space runs out after 2038.",
